%description:

Tcp.softIcmpErrorsAbortSetup:linux-ipv6 -- over IPv6, a Time Exceeded aborts SYN_SENT.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "a soft ICMP error ... aborts the connection setup, as Linux".

The class linux-ipv6: TcpConnection::processIcmpv6Error() counts an ICMPv6 Time Exceeded, a
Destination Unreachable for no route or address, and a Parameter Problem as errors that abort
the setup when the value is true. This facet comes from the coverage gap loop: no test reached the code of this part. This test separates "linux" from "rfc" over IPv6, where
the SYN goes again.

Host under test: host1, on IPv6 nodes (precondition); the network is TapRouterNetwork, and the
tap sets the hop limit of the first SYN of host1 to 1, so the router sends a Time Exceeded. The
application of host1 opens at 3 s, after the address configuration. Observation: level 1, host1
sends no second SYN.

%# parameter: Tcp.softIcmpErrorsAbortSetup
%# class: linux-ipv6
%# value: true
%# key: *.host1.tcp.softIcmpErrorsAbortSetup
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpSoftIcmpErrorsAbortSetupLinuxIpv6")
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host1").filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true").nth(1).set("ipv6.hopLimit", "1")
                     .describe("the first SYN of host1: a hop limit of 1, so that the router sends a Time Exceeded"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(3.5))
        .never(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
              .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
              .describe("a second SYN of host1")
              .within(2.0));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpSoftIcmpErrorsAbortSetupLinuxIpv6 compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.softIcmpErrorsAbortSetup = true    # the parameter under test
*.host*.typename = "StandardHost6"
*.configurator.typename = "Ipv6NetworkConfigurator"
**.ipv6.configurator.networkConfiguratorModule = "configurator"
*.router.typename = "Router6"
network = inet.protocoltest.TapRouterNetwork
*.host1.app[0].tOpen = 3s
*.host1.app[0].tSend = 3.1s
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpSoftIcmpErrorsAbortSetupLinuxIpv6: PASS
